WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.203
- I know tens of
thousands of people,

00:00:02.203 --> 00:00:03.878
and I know thousands
of people extremely well,

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:06.347
and I know hundreds
of people deeply well.

00:00:06.347 --> 00:00:09.517
There is no correlation
between how much money

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:12.019
someone makes and
their level of happiness.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:15.489
I have friends who
make $47,000 a year,

00:00:15.489 --> 00:00:17.358
and they're the
happiest people I know.

00:00:17.358 --> 00:00:19.506
Their work-life
balance is on point,

00:00:19.506 --> 00:00:21.341
they're part of
two soccer teams,

00:00:21.341 --> 00:00:22.379
they play video games,

00:00:22.379 --> 00:00:23.771
they watch every show they want,

00:00:23.771 --> 00:00:26.006
they take two vacations
that they scrap together,

00:00:26.006 --> 00:00:28.109
and they're
freaking happy as well.

00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:30.077
And I know tons of
people who I grew up with

00:00:30.077 --> 00:00:32.813
in the Silicon Valley
boom who have hundreds

00:00:32.813 --> 00:00:35.149
of millions of dollars 
in their bank account

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:37.084
and are as
miserable and as lonely

00:00:37.084 --> 00:00:38.886
and as broken
as you'll ever see,

00:00:38.886 --> 00:00:43.758
so I implore all of you
to please reverse engineer

00:00:43.758 --> 00:00:45.292
and figure out who you are,

00:00:45.292 --> 00:00:50.231
and figure out what level of
monetizing and stuff you need,

00:00:50.231 --> 00:00:52.233
and what level of
creativity you need.

00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:53.134
I promise you one thing,

00:00:53.134 --> 00:00:56.337
one thing that will
catch you very off-guard.

00:00:56.337 --> 00:00:58.806
I should be way more rich.

00:00:58.806 --> 00:01:01.509
I leave money on
the table every day.

00:01:01.509 --> 00:01:04.512
I've left ungodly amounts
of money on the table.

00:01:04.512 --> 00:01:08.182
I spend tons of time sending DMs

00:01:08.182 --> 00:01:10.551
and engaging with people
and meeting people randomly

00:01:10.551 --> 00:01:11.719
and not cashing in.

00:01:11.719 --> 00:01:14.755
I actually believe the
statement I'm about to make.

00:01:14.755 --> 00:01:17.892
I think that I love
the journey and the game

00:01:17.892 --> 00:01:19.926
of entrepreneurship so much

00:01:19.926 --> 00:01:24.565
that I have subconsciously
sabotaged my financial upside

00:01:24.565 --> 00:01:26.467
to make sure I can
play this a little longer,

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:28.602
'cause I fear if the
numbers keep getting too big,

00:01:28.602 --> 00:01:32.239
eventually, it will
take the fun out of it.

00:01:32.239 --> 00:01:34.508
When you are
lucky enough like I am

00:01:34.508 --> 00:01:37.812
to actually do something
that you love so much,

00:01:37.812 --> 00:01:41.649
do something that puts
pressure against the one thing

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:42.917
you care about besides it,

00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:45.052
which is the time
I spend with my family.

00:01:45.052 --> 00:01:46.387
My family's my whole life,

00:01:46.387 --> 00:01:49.356
and being this and doing this

00:01:49.356 --> 00:01:51.559
is the only thing
that cuts into that.

00:01:51.559 --> 00:01:54.995
I couldn't breathe if
I wasn't an entrepreneur.

00:01:54.995 --> 00:01:57.898
I didn't breathe when
I wasn't an entrepreneur.

00:01:57.898 --> 00:02:00.434
That's the reason I got
D's and F's in school.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.536
'Cause I just couldn't be me,

00:02:02.536 --> 00:02:04.371
and I'm not capable of that.

00:02:04.371 --> 00:02:07.875
And so, I think
being here excites me

00:02:07.875 --> 00:02:11.512
because I think coming
to not L.A., San Francisco,

00:02:11.512 --> 00:02:13.781
New York, London, is
always more fun for me.

00:02:13.781 --> 00:02:15.716
It always feels a
little more practical.

00:02:15.716 --> 00:02:17.184
It always feels like
there's a little bit more

00:02:17.184 --> 00:02:20.254
chips on the shoulder,
which is what I have.

00:02:20.254 --> 00:02:22.056
But I wanna remind everybody,

00:02:22.056 --> 00:02:23.958
just 'cause you didn't
grow up with a trust fund,

00:02:23.958 --> 00:02:26.794
just 'cause you don't
live in Silicon Valley,

00:02:26.794 --> 00:02:28.769
the market doesn't care.

00:02:28.769 --> 00:02:30.475
If you're good
enough, you will win,

00:02:30.475 --> 00:02:33.580
(light hip hop beat)

